  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity under preparation SWIOP grant to Indian Ocean Commission - &quot;Support toward the activities of the Indian Ocean Commission (IOC) Sub-Regional Fisheries Monitoring Control, Surveillance, and Observation  Coordination Centre (FMCSOCC)&quot;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;General objective:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;Ocean and water governance is enhanced in terms of regional/international cooperation and coordination on policies, Monitoring, Control and Surveillance, research and data sharing for better decision making and sustainable management and inclusive use of ocean and water resources.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Specific Objectives:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;Strengthen the IOC FMCSOCC regional actions to prevent, deter, and eliminate IUU fishing in the Southwestern Indian Ocean in the context of institutionalizing the Regional Fisheries Surveillance Plan (PRSP);  Resulting in strengthening this unique regional collaboration through support for joint deployment of patrol resources of the participating states of the FMCSOCC and the promotion and strengthening of exchanges of fisheries data and intelligence between coastal states, for the purpose of MCS. In collaboration with existing regional fisheries MCS and regional maritime security organisations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
